  "uprn": "100023491716",
  "decision_date": "12/04/2006",
  "description": "Demolition of existing shops/ offices/ flats and erection of a four storey block comprising 10 x one bed and 6 x two bed flats and erection of new front garden wall.",
  "site_name": "331-335",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "27/06/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "Chiswick High Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "11/04/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the flats are occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Friday  and none shall take place on Saturdays, Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - The waste and recycled materials storage arrangements shown on the approved drawing shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 6 - The erection of the flats shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound between the flats, and between adjoining properties has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  These details shall include proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure to the front and rear of the site, hard surfacing material in the front, refuse and recycling units,  privacy screens. \r\n\r\nSoft landscape works shall include planting plans; written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment); schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before the flats are occupied or in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 9 - Before the development hereby permitted is commenced a scheme indicating the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to and within the flats and to the rear garden shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use.",
    "Condition : 10 - 11.\tNo development shall take place until the applicant has secured the implementation of a program of archaeological work, in accordance with a written scheme of investigation which has been submitted by the applicant and approved by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 11 - In this condition \"retained tree\" means an existing tree which is to be retained in accordance with the approved plans and particulars; and paragraphs (a) and (b) below shall have effect until the expiration of (5 years?) from the date of the occupation of the flats\r\n\r\n(a)\tNo retained tree shall be cut down, uprooted or destroyed, nor shall any retained tree be topped or lopped other than in accordance with the approved plans and particulars, without the written approval of the local planning authority.  Any topping or lopping approved shall be carried out in accordance with British Standard[3998 (Tree Work)] or any other BS replacing.\r\n\r\n(b)\tIf any retained tree is removed, uprooted or destroyed or dies, another tree shall be planted at the same place and that tree shall be of such size and species, and shall be planted at such time, as may be specified in writing by the local planning authority.\r\n\r\n(c)\tThe erection of fencing for the protection of any retained tree shall be undertaken in accordance with the approved plans and particulars and in accordance with BS 5837 Tree Protection, before any equipment, machinery or materials are brought on to the site for the purposes of the development, and shall be maintained until all equipment, machinery and surplus materials have been removed from the site.  Nothing shall be stored or placed in any area fenced in accordance with this condition and the ground levels within those areas shall not be altered, nor shall any excavation be made, without the written consent of the local planning authority.",
    "Condition : 12 - 13.\tDevelopment shall not commence until a survey of the existing ground levels has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. The approved ground levels shall not be raised or otherwise altered from those shown on the submitted plan, without the prior written approval of the Local Planning Authority",
    "Condition : 13 - 14.\tThe flats shall not be occupied until the area shown to be enclosed at the front of the building has been laid out in accordance with drawing no MMFD/30C, and all necessary consents obtained.",
    "Condition : 14 - The proposed development because of its position, design and appearance, is acceptable having due regard for the site characteristics. The proposal would have a positive impact on appearance of the locality, and would not harm nearby neighbours living conditions. The development is in accordance with policies ENVB.1.1 (New Development), H 1.1 (Location of New Housing), H 4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H 4.2 (Residential Density) and T 1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities for Developments)."
  ],
